The module manages one immutable inventory reservation line. `createReservationLine` requires a nonblank SKU after trimming, a finite unit cost at least zero, and an integer quantity from 1 through 25. It preserves the SKU and label exactly and returns a new object. `withReservationQuantity` applies the same quantity bounds, returns the original line when unchanged, and otherwise returns a new line without mutating the input. `reservationTotal` returns unit cost times quantity.

`removeReservation` removes every line whose SKU exactly equals the requested SKU, preserving relative order of remaining lines. It returns the original readonly array when there is no match; otherwise it returns a new array. It never mutates the input. Duplicate SKUs are permitted. Empty input is valid. Empty lookup SKUs are ordinary lookup values even though valid created lines cannot have blank SKUs. Floating-point arithmetic uses ordinary JavaScript number semantics.

